  "type": "text",
  "prompt": "Compute the number of pairs of 2011-tuples $(x_1,x_2,\\dots,x_{2011})$ and $(y_1,y_2,\\dots,y_{2011})$ such that $x_{k+1}=x_k^2-y_k^2-2$ and $y_{k+1}=2x_ky_k$ for $1\\le k\\le2010$, $x_1=x_{2011}^2-y_{2011}^2-2$, and $y_1=2x_{2011}y_{2011}$.",
  "image": null,
  "choices": null,
  "answer": "2^2011",
  "acceptedAnswers": [
   "2^{2011}",
   "2**2011"
  ],
  "answerUnit": null,
  "solutions": [],
  "topics": [
   "algebra",
   "complex-numbers",
   "counting"
  ],
  "difficulty": 3,
  "duplicateOf": "smt-2011-team-13",
  "reviewNote": "The paper prints the recursion as x_k = x_{k-1}^2 - y_{k-1}^2 - 2 for 1 <= k <= 2010 (the indices do not fit); it is stated here with x_{k+1}, y_{k+1} for 1 <= k <= 2010, which is the intended cyclic system. The tuples are taken to be complex, as in the official solution."
